471-## Example numbers by case
472-
473-The triggers in B1 and K3 are comparisons. The measurement decides them, so no number is fixed in advance. This
474-section shows **what those comparisons have come out at elsewhere**, by agent type and condition, so a reader knows
475-roughly where a project stands before measuring. These are examples with sources, not thresholds. The first
476-subsection is different: it gives start-file limits, which `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` Rd3 uses for the `INDEX.md` size
477-check. No cache trigger compares them.
478-
479-Run: `runs/20261012-caches-numbers/`. Its source ids are:
480-- `W-*`: web research (`nodes/web.md`);
481-- `OC`: opencode's research (`nodes/opencode.md`);
482-- `SZ`: the SEZA measurement (`nodes/seza.md`; every number with its command);
483-- `CX`: codex's independent second look at SEZA, by agent type (`nodes/codex.md`);
484-- `BM-*`, `S-F*`, `V-F*`, `G-F*`, `s3-F*`: as above.
485-
486-Web quotes are model-made extracts, not byte-checked, except W-1. Numbers marked *my arithmetic* are computed from a
487-sourced figure.
