489-### The index read at session start (`INDEX.md`, `MEMORY.md`), by agent type
490-
491-| Agent | Window | Limit on files loaded at start | Measured effective context | Example |
492-|---|---|---|---|---|
493-| Claude Code (Claude 5.x) | 1M (W-8) | `MEMORY.md`: "first 200 lines … or the first 25KB, whichever comes first"; `CLAUDE.md`: target under 200 lines (W-1) | Opus 4.6, MRCR v2: 76% at 1M (W-14); 93% at 256K (W-15, reported) | 25 KB binds first: about 150 lines at 167 B per line (W-1), about 107 lines at SEZA's 233 B per line (*my arithmetic*, SZ) |
494-| Codex (GPT-6.x) | 1.05M per the API (W-9), but this machine's Codex model cache says `context_window: 500000`, 95% effective, so about 475K (CX) | `AGENTS.md` combined up to 32 KiB (`project_doc_max_bytes`) (W-2) | GPT-5.4: 79.3% at 128K–256K, 36.6% at 512K–1M (W-15, reported) | instructions plus index under 32 KiB, if the index is loaded through `AGENTS.md` |
495-| agy (Gemini 3.1 Pro / 3.8 Flash) | 1,048,576 (W-9, CX) | 24,000 bytes per rule file, **and** a 20,000-token budget across all rules (CX, official page); 12,000 characters in other reports (W-4, conflict) | 84.9% at 128K, 26.3% at 1M (W-15, reported) | under 12,000 characters if both readings must hold (*my reading*) |
496-| opencode (MiniMax M3 / M2.7) | 1M / 204,800 (W-9) | no limit stated (W-6) | GAP | follow the strictest agent sharing the repo |
497-| dsh (DeepSeek flash / V4 pro) | 1,048,576 (CX) | a 65,536-byte budget for the instruction files it loads (CX, from its loader docs) | GAP | instructions plus index under 64 KiB, if the index is loaded through its instruction files |
498-| Qwen Code | — | its auto-memory index is capped at 200 lines or 25,000 bytes (`MAX_MANAGED_AUTO_MEMORY_INDEX_LINES` / `_BYTES`, CX); it also warns when always-loaded context passes 15% of the window, an advisory only (CX) | — | the index cap binds first: under 25,000 bytes, as for Claude |
499-| Cursor | — | rules "under 500 lines" (W-3) | — | — |
