15:## Where they agree
16-
17-- **The tool reports a result other than pass or fail for what it cannot decide.** Linus: "Missing evidence produces an
18-  incomplete result, never a pass"; 范蠡: reviewer items are "never report[ed] as pass or fail"; 孫子: "'not checked' for a
19-  stage that never ran"; 老子: "one `unknown` state, never folded into pass"; Dave: "*needs a reviewer*, never as pass";
20-  Dario: results for "partly checked", "guidance", "break found, reason not looked for" and "could not run" (*quoted*,
21-  all six). The names of the extra results differ (*my reading*; see disagreements).
22-- **W2.1b, W5.1 and K1.1 cannot be decided from git, despite their `git` label.** All six say so (*quoted*: Linus "It
23-  cannot determine generally whether a code change embodies a new decision"; 范蠡 lists them under "Need what the tool
24-  cannot see"; 孫子, 老子, Dave and Dario list them as reviewer or not buildable).
25-- **`memory_index.py --check` reads the staging area or a commit, not the working tree.** Linus, 范蠡, 孫子, Dave, Dario
26-  (*quoted*). 老子 adds only that it takes no path and runs on the cwd's git root (*quoted*). So the report must name its
27-  snapshot — Linus, 孫子, Dave say this outright (*quoted*).
28-- **Reuse `memory_index.py` (C3) rather than rewrite it.** All six (*quoted*). How much it covers is disputed (below).
29-- **SHOULD records with "with no written reason" cannot be failed by a tool.** Linus, 孫子, 老子, Dave, Dario (*quoted*);
30-  老子 calls it "the largest gap in the four docs" (*quoted*). 范蠡 does not raise it (*my reading*).
31-- **Records that mix a mechanical and a reviewer check have no result rule today.** Linus, 孫子, 老子, Dave, Dario
32-  (*quoted*). 孫子 and Dave give the same rule: a mechanical fail is a fail; otherwise any human half means needs a
33-  reviewer (*quoted*).
34-- **CACHES Core requirements have no `check` field (and no levels), and most of them are runtime behaviour.** Linus,
35-  孫子, Dave, Dario (*quoted*); 范蠡 agrees on the runtime half only (B2.1, B3.1, B5.1, K2, Rd3) (*quoted*).
36-- **"Required location" (C4, R2) has no source in the guidelines; this repo has no `project-memory/`.** All six raise
37-  the absent-memory case (*quoted*); what to do about it is disputed (below).
38-- **U5's `git status --short` is too weak; hash the whole tree, ignored files included.** Linus, 孫子, Dave, Dario
39-  (*quoted*). 孫子, Dave and Dario add `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` on git calls (*quoted*).
40-- **F1 needs a home-folder override so tests do not touch the real home; U1's "user memory" has no path in the
41-  guidelines.** Linus, 孫子, Dave, Dario (*quoted*).
42-- **Tests: the expected answer is written before the check, by hand or by another route, never computed by the check.**
43-  All six (*quoted*). Dave and Dario add a sabotage step: remove or force-pass each check and a test must go red
44-  (*quoted*); 孫子 a "mutation check" that flips one expected row (*quoted*).
45-- **Build in small pieces, hook last, hook installed only on EJ's yes to the settings diff.** All six (*quoted*).
