`memory-check` v1 is built and verified.

**What exists** — `memory_check/` (12 TS files, ~1,575 lines): a guideline loader (the tool's own verbatim copy of the SoT YAML + `CACHES.md`, version = content hashes), F1/F2 locations, a `tools/memory_index.py --check` adapter that maps each of its messages to a requirement id (C3 — never judged a second way), the tool's own git clauses (W1.1a's unseen prefix clause, W6.1a, K4.1, K4.3, the rename halves of W1.1a/b), the C6 v1 cache checks (B2.2 by `git check-ignore`, Rd1.1 by a session-start scan), the report, the warning and the CLI.

**Verified** — `tsgo --noEmit -p .` clean; smoke run on this repo exits 0 (`runs/20261017-memory-check/nodes/smoke-report.md`; one real fail: `CACHES:B2`/B2.2 — `.cache` is not gitignored here). All 64 SoT records and 11 CACHES requirements appear with one of the five states, every one with evidence. Six throwaway fixtures confirmed each planted break is found, that reads change nothing (status + md5sums before/after), that usage errors exit 2, that a shallow clone makes history MUSTs "could not run", and that a missing `AGENTS.md` warns and exits 1.

**Two contradictions reported** in `implement.result.md`: U2's "exactly that requirement" cannot hold for K6.1a/K6.2 (one comparison, both ids — `research-q/compare.md` §7 names this); and R2's warning clause conflicts with its reduced-scope hook clause, so `--warn` prints every failing MUST and the hook is left uninstalled (owner's, R12.3). Also noted: `CACHES.md` gives its requirements no level, so a failing cache requirement cannot gate the exit code under R3.
